# VICTOR — environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env (repository root) and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit
# real credentials.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is required to run VICTOR locally. With all of it unset the app
# runs fully offline on committed data — which is the demo path. These variables
# turn on persistence, object storage and the LLM briefing.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase — database
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Connection string for the computation store and route cache.
#
# USE THE POOLER (port 6543), not the direct connection (5432). Supabase's
# pgbouncer pooler tolerates the connection churn a free-tier Render instance
# produces — it spins down after 15 minutes idle and reconnects on wake. The
# direct connection has a low connection cap and drops idle sessions, which is
# exactly the failure mode the store's reconnect logic exists to absorb.
#
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string →
# "Connection pooling" → Transaction mode.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Direct connection (port 5432) — for APPLYING MIGRATIONS ONLY.
# pgbouncer in transaction mode does not reliably support every DDL statement.
#   psql "$DIRECT_DATABASE_URL" -f supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql
#
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# How long persisted computations and cached routes are kept, in seconds.
# Default is 7 days. Keeps the free tier's 500 MB database bounded.
# COMPUTATION_TTL_SECONDS=604800

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase — object storage (map tiles)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Used by scripts/upload_tiles.py only. Never needed at runtime by the API,
# and never by the frontend.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# The service_role key, NOT the anon key. It bypasses Row Level Security, so it
# must stay server-side — never expose it to the browser or commit it.
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=<service-role-key>

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend — CORS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Primary browser origin allowed to call the API. localhost is always permitted
# in addition to this, so local development keeps working against a deployed
# backend.
# FRONTEND_URL=https://victor-web.onrender.com

# Optional comma-separated extra origins (preview deploys, a custom domain).
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://preview-victor.onrender.com,https://victor.example.com

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend — optional LLM mission briefing
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Without a key the briefing generator falls back to a deterministic template
# that produces a complete brief offline. The demo must never depend on this.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend — set these on the WEB SERVICE, not here
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* at build time, so changing either requires a
# redeploy of the web service, not just a restart.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://victor-api.onrender.com
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_BASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/victor-tiles
#
# Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_BASE_URL unset to serve tiles from the API instead.
# That is correct for local development and for the offline demo; it is wrong
# in production, where Render's ephemeral filesystem loses the tiles on every
# redeploy.
